    <article>
      <section id="hello" class="doc-hero"><span class="pill">THE SOULI FIELD GUIDE · V2.7</span><h1>A little world.<br>A soul of its own.</h1><p class="lede">A token that draws a fren. A fren that makes a home.<br>A quiet corner of Base that keeps growing with you.</p><div class="hero-art" aria-label="Original SOULI inscription samples"><img v-for="s in souls.slice(0,5)" :key="s.label" :src="s.url" :alt="s.label"><span>24 × 24 pixels.<br>Plenty of personality.</span></div><p>SOULI starts with an existing ERC-20i token and its original 24 × 24 on-chain art. Connect to see and share your inscription today. A new automatic 3D world is in development; the original inscription stays the source of your character’s identity.</p><div class="quick-grid"><div><strong>Meet your SOULI</strong><span>Connect to see your original art.</span></div><div><strong>Bring your inscription</strong><span>The original pixels are the character.</span></div><div><strong>Grow at your pace</strong><span>A tiny dot belongs here too.</span></div></div><div class="note"><b>Read this as a living plan.</b> The game is cooking. An early 2D prototype and experimental holder services are separate from the new 3D game. The purchase page now checks current Base availability; the recorded mainnet check ended paused and empty. The first-sale 50:50 policy and 4.2M cap are approved. The fixed ETH price and real V2 receipts are published below. The first stock target is 1.4M, with another 2.8M available for later restocking. The first 1,399,999 SOULI were funded and the operator opened the sale on October 4, 2026 at 05:29 UTC. Check the purchase page for current stock and status. Allocation reconciliation and the LP schedule remain unfinished.</div></section>

      <section id="inscriptions"><p class="eyebrow">01 / ORIGINAL ART. ON BASE.</p><h2>A token with a little soul.</h2><p class="lede">An inscription is the character information carried by the SOULI token system.</p><p>Most tokens tell you how much you hold. SOULI can also show you a character. The contract uses a whole-token <b>seed</b> and additional inscription data to choose pixel shapes and colors. Its renderer produces a 24 × 24 SVG: a small drawing described in code, rather than a photograph our game server invents.</p><div class="flow"><div><b>SOULI tokens</b><small>Transfer & balance rules</small></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><b>Seed + extra data</b><small>Stored inscription state</small></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><b>Your little fren</b><small>Rendered by the contract</small></div></div><p>We call this format <b>ERC-20i</b>: ERC-20 with native inscriptions. The balances remain fungible tokens; the associated art gives those balances personality. The character is not a separately minted ERC-721 NFT. ERC-20i is the inscription format pioneered by FUNGI, not a claim of an independently standardized ERC.</p>
      <div class="credit-card"><span class="eyebrow">ROOTED IN FUNGI</span><h3>Credit where it grew.</h3><p>SOULI builds on the ERC-20i native-inscription approach pioneered by <b>FUNGI</b> and <b>Todd Stool (ToddStool.eth)</b>. We credit their original inscription mechanics, layered on-chain art framework and published code. SOULI adds its own world, game experience and product direction; we do not claim to have invented ERC-20i.</p><a href="https://github.com/ToddStool/fungi">Explore the original FUNGI project ↗</a><p class="caption">Independent project. This credit does not imply a partnership, endorsement or security review by FUNGI or Todd Stool.</p></div><h3>Why it feels different</h3><div class="two-cards"><div><h4>Discover a form</h4><p>A changing seed can reveal a different body, palette or effect. Collecting becomes a personal choice about the form you like, not a promise of rarity or resale value.</p></div><div><h4>Give it a place to live</h4><p>The same inscription you can inspect on Base becomes your resident. The game adds movement, a home and shared stories around that original art.</p></div></div><p>The artwork layers include background, ground, body or essence, eyes and effects. Not every level uses every layer. Game-side floating and light effects are presentation; they do not rewrite the inscription or turn a game animation into an on-chain transaction.</p>
      <div class="note"><b>Your amount sets the level. The contract generates the look.</b> For a new Dynamic soul, the minimum seed amounts are 1 / 21,000 / 150,000 / 500,000 / 2,500,000 SOULI for levels 1–5. Two new souls at level 4 can have different bodies, colors and effects. You buy token units, not a chosen example character.</div><p>Adding or removing whole SOULI from a Dynamic seed updates its inscription data and can change the appearance even within the same level. Exact results depend on the transfer route and existing inscriptions. The renderer is deterministic for the same seed data; it does not promise a unique, equally likely or brand-new random outcome on every purchase.</p><div class="level-demo"><div><span class="eyebrow">EXPLORE THE ORIGINAL RENDERER</span><h3>Even a dot is a fren.</h3><div class="level-buttons" role="group" aria-label="Inscription level preview"><button v-for="(item,i) in levels.levels" :key="i" :aria-pressed="i===selectedLevel" @click="selectedLevel=i">{{i===0?'Dot':'Lv '+item.displayLevel}}</button></div><p aria-live="polite"><b>Level {{soul.displayLevel}}</b> · minimum seed <b>{{Number(soul.minimum).toLocaleString('en-US')}} SOULI</b></p><small>Single-seed thresholds, not the sum of all inscriptions in a wallet. Samples do not guarantee a purchase outcome.</small></div><figure><img :src="svgUrl(soul.svg)" :alt="'Original on-chain renderer sample for level '+soul.displayLevel"><figcaption>Base renderer snapshot<br>Block {{levels.block.toLocaleString('en-US')}}</figcaption></figure></div>
      <div class="two-cards"><div><h4>Dynamic: room to become</h4><p>Receiving or spending SOULI can change the dynamic seed and its art. Adding tokens may reach a new artwork level; it does not guarantee a particular face or color.</p></div><div><h4>Stable: a form to keep</h4><p>Transfer exactly the whole-token amount of that inscription to a qualifying different wallet to preserve its seed and appearance as Stable. It is still part of the token system. Spending the associated tokens can affect it; “Stable” does not mean locked forever.</p></div></div><details><summary>Before transferring a favorite form</summary><p>The transfer path depends on the seed amount, dynamic/stable state, recipient holdings and special pool addresses. An exact seed match can preserve stored seed data when the recipient does not already hold that seed. Arbitrary partial transfers are not a preservation method. The original contract can consume or change inscription state as tokens are spent.</p><p>The current preview does not offer preservation transfers. Inspect both wallets and the exact contract behavior before moving a favorite. The renderer and artwork administration also matter: on-chain storage does not prove that all artwork settings are permanently unchangeable.</p></details><p class="caption">The original PDF described six levels and included legacy terminology. This guide uses the five display levels (1–5, contract levels 0–4) observed in the deployed renderer on October 1, 2026. The dated snapshot is not a promise that admin-controlled settings can never change.</p></section>

      <section id="world"><p class="eyebrow">02 / WORLD STATUS: COOKING.</p><h2>A little world.<br>Still in the making.</h2><p>The current direction is a miniature 3D world with automatic gathering and cooperative defense. Your original 2D inscription informs the game character. A game-side 3D model is a presentation of that art, not a new on-chain asset or a replacement for the original renderer.</p><blockquote>“ETH is down. Your SOULI found a glowing stone.<br>The town used it to light another lamp.”<strong>Market red. Our little town got brighter.</strong></blockquote><p>This is a design example. ETH-linked atmosphere, short stories and low-input cooperation remain part of the direction; their final implementation can change. Buying SOULI does not guarantee a finished game, access, a release date or token rewards.</p><div class="quick-grid"><div><strong>Today</strong><span>View and share your original inscription.</span></div><div><strong>In development</strong><span>An automatic 3D world for little souls.</span></div><div><strong>Same tiny fren</strong><span>A level-one dot belongs here too.</span></div></div><h3>Art level is not game progress</h3><p>A larger token balance can change the inscription’s form. It should not make a high art level the entry ticket to an enjoyable game. The specific game balance and holder benefits are still being designed.</p><details><summary>What about the earlier preview?</summary><p>The early 2D prototype supports local progress and sample visitors. Experimental saved homes and asynchronous cooperation belong to that prototype, not to a finished 3D release. Live avatars, chat and open invitations are not a published game feature.</p><a href="/lighthouse.html">Try the early 2D prototype ↗</a></details><a class="button" href="/soul/">Meet my SOULI ↗</a></section>

      <section id="tokenomics"><p class="eyebrow">03 / NUMBERS YOU CAN READ.</p><h2>One existing token.<br>A new place to use it.</h2><div class="metric-row"><div><strong>210,000,000</strong><span>SOULI supply at the recorded block</span></div><div><strong>Base · 9 decimals</strong><span>Existing ERC-20i token</span></div></div><p>The game uses the existing SOULI token. This plan does not issue a replacement supply. At <a :href="'https://basescan.org/block/'+facts.block">block {{facts.block.toLocaleString('en-US')}}</a>, the supply was 210 million. Circulating supply and the full set of team-controlled wallets are still being reconciled.</p><div class="address-box"><span>Real SOULI · Base mainnet 8453</span><a :href="'https://basescan.org/token/'+TOKEN">{{TOKEN}} ↗</a><small>Verify the entire address. This is not a payment address.</small></div><h3>50% liquidity. 50% building.</h3><span class="pill proposal">APPROVED POLICY · CHECK LIVE AVAILABILITY</span><p>The first round is capped at <b>4,200,000 SOULI</b>, with <b>no calendar deadline</b>. There is no extra per-wallet limit: one wallet may buy all remaining stock. Half of actual purchase ETH is allocated to manual LP, with separate matching SOULI; half funds project operations. Operators can pause the sale and recover unsold stock. Selling out is the target, not a promise that the sale will stay open indefinitely.</p><p>Start with a <b>1,400,000 SOULI cumulative stock target</b>, including the one-token mainnet check. At the original reference price this is about <b>$100,000 gross</b>. Another <b>2,800,000 SOULI</b> can be added in batches while selling, within the same 4.2M cap. The first target is an inventory plan, not a new on-chain limit. One buyer may buy all currently available stock.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Original reference arithmetic · USD values move with ETH</caption><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>First stock target</th><th>Full round</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>SOULI sold · cumulative</td><td>1,400,000</td><td>4,200,000</td></tr><tr><td>Reference gross</td><td>$100,000</td><td>$300,000</td></tr><tr><td>Purchase ETH · fixed rate</td><td>37.3324473099172</td><td>111.9973419297516</td></tr><tr><td>50% for LP · ETH side</td><td>18.6662236549586 ETH · reference $50,000</td><td>55.9986709648758 ETH · reference $150,000</td></tr><tr><td>Separate matching SOULI</td><td>700,000 · reference $50,000</td><td>2,100,000 · reference $150,000</td></tr><tr><td>Both sides of LP · reference</td><td>$100,000</td><td>$300,000</td></tr><tr><td>50% for operations · reference</td><td>$50,000 before costs</td><td>$150,000 before costs</td></tr><tr><td>Sold + matching LP stock</td><td>2,100,000 · 1% of total supply</td><td>6,300,000 · 3% of total supply</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The reference price is $15M divided by 210M tokens, about $0.07142857 each. LP examples assume the same initial price; the actual pool ratio and existing reserves must be reviewed at execution. Matching tokens come from a separate reserve, not the SOULI delivered to buyers. Additional sales keep the same 50:50 policy; the first LP budget does not make later proceeds entirely operating income.</p><p>FDV is price multiplied by total supply, not cash raised or an established market valuation. The SOULI half of an LP is not extra cash. Its initial value comes from the pool ratio, and trading changes that ratio. Small liquidity relative to FDV can produce large price moves; no exit price is guaranteed.</p><h3>The sale on Base</h3><p>V2 is deployed with a fixed price of <b>0.000026666033792798 ETH per SOULI</b> (26,666,033,792,798 wei). The reference was ETH/USD 2,678.635 on October 3, 2026 at 13:19:46 UTC, using a $15M FDV and 210M supply. The sale and wallet caps are both 4.2M; no calendar deadline applies. A phone purchase and the stock/proceeds recovery cycle completed on this exact V2. The production purchase and management pages use this same verified V2. The first production stock was deposited and the sale opened on October 4, 2026 at 05:29 UTC. Those receipts are published below. Current availability appears on the purchase page. Internal checks are completed; no independent audit was performed.</p><p>ETH/USD changes move the dollar equivalent of a fixed-ETH sale. A target is not a live dollar cap. The 4.2M round has a fixed cumulative token cap. Restocking within that cap uses the existing contract; selling beyond it needs a new disclosed round and contract. There is no automatic overflow round. The ETH rate is fixed on chain. No calendar deadline does not guarantee a fixed USD price.</p><details><summary>Why high art levels cannot be gameplay requirements</summary><p>At the reference price, a 21,000-token seed would cost about $1,500 and a 2,500,000-token seed about $178,571. These are arithmetic illustrations, not quotes. The lowest form must remain a complete resident, and the free preview must stand on its own. Purchasing a high art level is optional collecting, not the entry ticket to an enjoyable game.</p></details></section>

      <section id="allocation"><p class="eyebrow">04 / A BUDGET, WITH CLEAR LIMITS.</p><h2>Build for the long game.</h2><span class="pill proposal">TEAM TARGET · NOT A HOLDINGS REPORT</span><p>The founder and team budget target is <b>15% of total supply: 31,500,000 SOULI</b>. This replaces the earlier proposal based on a percentage of the remaining reserve. It is not a new mint or a claim that those tokens have already been allocated or locked.</p><div class="allocation-bar" aria-hidden="true"><span v-for="a in allocations" :key="a.name" :style="{width:a.percent+'%',background:a.color}"></span></div><div class="allocation-list"><div v-for="a in allocations" :key="a.name"><strong :style="{borderColor:a.color}">{{a.percent}}% <span>{{a.name}}</span></strong><p>{{a.text}}</p></div></div><div class="note"><b>Wallet control and compensation are different.</b> Team-controlled ecosystem or operating reserves must also be disclosed. A 15% compensation target does not mean the team controls only 15% of the supply.</div><p>Balances outside the main reserve wallet are not automatically team distributions. Wallet ownership and prior investor commitments remain under review. They cannot be counted both as existing holder allocations and as additional team grants. No allocation or vesting lock is deployed by this page.</p><h3>Release gradually, with receipts</h3><p>Proposed team release at launch: zero. One candidate first tranche is at most <b>210,000 SOULI</b>, with a 12-month cliff followed by 24 months of linear release and no catch-up lump sum. It is part of the 31,500,000-token target, not an extra allocation. Dates, beneficiaries and contracts remain unapproved and unimplemented.</p><p>A confirmed schedule must show the beneficiary, contract, funded balance, dates and who can change or revoke it. Existing holders keep their rights. The rest of the allocation will be specified after those holdings and obligations are reconciled.</p><h3>Keep the lights on, honestly</h3><p>Free exploration and optional inscription ownership come first. Paid homes, furniture and seasonal decorations are future product proposals. The approved first-sale policy uses 50% of purchase ETH for manual LP and 50% for operations. Development, security reviews, marketing, hosting, gas, tax and reserves must fit within the operating half; the detailed spending plan is pending. The 4.2M sale stock and up to 2.1M LP stock are separate from the team compensation target and must not be counted twice. Token reserves are not cash runway. No price appreciation or token rewards are promised.</p></section>

      <section id="funds"><p class="eyebrow">05 / CHECK THE PATH. KNOW THE KEYS.</p><h2>Follow the funds.</h2><SaleProof /><div class="flow"><div><b>You buy with ETH</b><small>SOULI arrives in the same successful transaction</small></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><b>Sale contract holds ETH</b><small>Registered operators can withdraw</small></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><b>Team adds liquidity</b><small>A separate manual Uniswap transaction</small></div></div><div class="note"><b>One of three operator wallets is enough.</b> The deployed controller gives each of three registered wallets independent control. This is not two-of-three approval and does not use Safe. Losing one wallet leaves the others available; compromising any one wallet can expose all funds under this authority.</div><p>Each deployed controller owns its corresponding sale and receives its proceeds. Any registered operator can pause or resume that sale, fund stock, recover unsold stock while paused, or collect proceeds to the calling registered wallet. It cannot recover tokens already held in a lost personal wallet, undo a confirmed transfer, or replace a missing recovery phrase.</p><p>The current V2 receipts appear above. Earlier V1 and Base Sepolia shops are separate contracts with separate inventories. The historical V1 check also funded 42 original SOULI, sold 1, returned 41 and collected ETH. The buyer held 1 SOULI after that earlier check and 2 after the later V2 purchase. Neither collection was an LP deposit. <a href="/testnet/#three-wallet">Open the separate testnet shop ↗</a></p><details><summary>Earlier V1 receipts · historical</summary><p><a href="https://basescan.org/address/0x83bcB8Ba9b7518CDEc32f2eE0e684f1d7b4ffB01">Sale contract ↗</a> · <a href="https://basescan.org/address/0xD643520BfEb76e59250d56Df8B196F9c751Bc252">Controller ↗</a></p><p><a href="https://basescan.org/tx/0xa5c53410b5af2935dcab5e2bb6f9ebc5b59b6cfbc26083953821f01ce85234d5">1 SOULI purchased ↗</a><br><a href="https://basescan.org/tx/0x0e70c838a1a137b329e5b50fca8dccf5c2f04008e46e56f08ab4c7f5537e2563">41 unsold SOULI recovered ↗</a><br><a href="https://basescan.org/tx/0x2f955eb0cb8f6d9d17d823f635ae93275f9a63a9b1edbd4c4e88b99a9fd69316">0.000026684264049332 ETH collected ↗</a></p><p>Source code is verified. These receipts demonstrate a small completed purchase-and-recovery cycle, not an independent audit or a full commercial launch.</p></details><p class="caption">The pilot and testnet are separate contracts with separate inventories.</p><h3>LP is a manual operating plan</h3><p>The approved policy allocates <b>50% of actual purchase ETH to LP and 50% to operations</b>. Matching SOULI is separate from buyer inventory. This is a use-of-proceeds commitment; it is not a technical lock. The contracts do <b>not</b> restrict withdrawn ETH to Uniswap. A full progress bar does not automatically create a pool. The operator makes that transaction and must publish the actual amounts, pool address and transaction receipt. The V2 terms hash records the policy; it cannot enforce how withdrawn ETH is spent.</p><p>LP timing is a separate decision; sellout is not an approved prerequisite. Before creating the first pool, pause the fixed-price sale and review the pool price, existing liquidity and any remaining sale inventory. An open fixed-price sale alongside a moving DEX price can invite arbitrage. The initial ratio and matching stock must be reviewed at execution.</p><p>SOULI is delivered on a successful purchase, so holders do not wait for an LP launch to use an eligible inscription. No protocol refund is planned after successful delivery. Failed token delivery should revert the purchase and payment together; the network may still charge gas. LP timing, a secondary market and resale are not guaranteed.</p><div class="two-cards"><div><h4>Money received ≠ money in LP</h4><p>Show cumulative sales, current sale balance, controller balance, withdrawals and actual LP deposits separately. Founder top-ups are not customer sales. Do not count the same ETH twice as it moves between addresses.</p></div><div><h4>A pool ≠ a locked pool</h4><p>LP tokens or a position NFT carry withdrawal rights. Publish the owner, position and any lock contract and expiry. The approved plan is to lock LP principal for one year after the first pool is created. Holding LP in an operator wallet is not a lock. The implementation candidate is unmodified OpenZeppelin 5.6.1 VestingWallet with duration zero and a fixed release timestamp, holding Base Uniswap V2 ERC-20 LP shares. Local tests and an actual Base-state fork cover deposit, early-release prevention, owner transfer, expiry and withdrawal of the underlying pair assets. This is internal validation, not an independent audit. No public lock is deployed or funded; the beneficiary and exact unlock time remain pending.</p></div></div><details><summary>LP lock rights, fees and later deposits</summary><p>V2 fees accrue inside the LP position and stay locked with the shares. Anyone may trigger release after expiry, but the current beneficiary receives the assets. The beneficiary can transfer that future right without shortening the lock. The sale controller is not a valid LP recovery wallet. The standard contract allows ownership renunciation; operators must not use it because funds can become unrecoverable.</p><p>Require at least 365 days between the actual first lock deposit and its release time. The exact date and deposit receipt must be checked before showing Locked. Later deposits into the same contract inherit its original expiry; they do not get a fresh year. A later round needs its own reviewed lock. V3/V4 position NFTs must not be sent to this ERC-20 lock.</p><a href="https://docs.openzeppelin.com/contracts/5.x/api/finance">OpenZeppelin VestingWallet documentation ↗</a></details><a class="button secondary" href="/#receipts">See project receipts ↗</a></section>

      <section id="technology"><p class="eyebrow">06 / WEB3 WHERE IT MATTERS.</p><h2>The chain owns the token.<br>The game brings it to life.</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>What lives where</caption><thead><tr><th>Base</th><th>Browser & minimal services</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>SOULI balances and inscription state</td><td>Rendering, movement and local free-play progress</td></tr><tr><td>Renderer calls and token transfers</td><td>ETH market-data cache and weather presentation</td></tr><tr><td>Deployed sales, payments and receipts</td><td>Invited holder sign-in, saved homes and asynchronous cooperation</td></tr><tr><td>LP positions once actually created</td><td>Static website and this field guide</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Players do not pay gas for every step, lamp or gathering tick. The site is served through Azure Static Web Apps; a small API handles features that need shared state. This keeps the game responsive and infrastructure modest. Hosted services, RPC availability and internet access are still dependencies.</p><p>The art is generated from on-chain data, but the hosted game is not a fully on-chain or immutable application. Old references to an IPFS frontend do not establish that this Azure release has a verified permanent IPFS copy. On-chain art administration remains part of the permission review.</p><h3>Wallet prompts should mean one clear thing</h3><p>Connecting exposes your public address and lets the app request wallet actions; it is not itself a payment. A sign-in message, token spending approval and transaction are separate requests. ETH purchases use the exact quoted payment plus network fees. Inventory funding uses a finite allowance for the intended stock, not an unlimited approval by default.</p><p>We never need a seed phrase or private key. Always verify the domain, chain and destination. Disconnecting a site does not revoke earlier token allowances. The mainnet token, a test token and a sale contract are different addresses.</p></section>

      <section id="roadmap"><p class="eyebrow">07 / WEN? HERE'S THE REAL STATUS.</p><h2>Show the work.</h2><div class="note"><b>Tokens now. A world in progress.</b> Purchases deliver the existing Base token before the full game is ready. Buying does not guarantee a finished game, beta access, a release date, exchange listing or returns. The recorded mainnet check ended paused and empty; use the purchase page for current status. The fixed V2 price and completed real purchase cycle are published. First production stock funding and the operator opening signature are confirmed. Later LP execution and beneficiary decisions remain outstanding. The founder chose internal review without an external-audit launch requirement; no independent audit is claimed.</div><div class="status-list"><div><span class="status live">Available</span><h3>Original inscriptions</h3><p>Base token and renderer reads, original art samples, and My SOULI viewing and sharing. The earlier 2D prototype remains an optional experiment.</p></div><div><span class="status planned">Cooking</span><h3>The new 3D game</h3><p>Miniature-world exploration and automatic cooperation are in development. Prior 2D saved-home experiments do not establish a completed 3D game. There is no announced release date.</p></div><div><span class="status beta">Public testnet</span><h3>Practice payments</h3><p>Base Sepolia tSOULI purchases, stock funding/recovery and proceeds withdrawal. An independent buyer purchased in the earlier shop; the current shop uses the three-operator controller. tSOULI has no inscription, monetary value or mainnet redemption.</p></div><div><span class="status beta">Deployed on testnet</span><h3>Three independent operator wallets</h3><p>Controller and sale deployed; registered wallets and compiled code checked. New-shop funding, A’s purchase and inventory recovery/restock, and B’s independent proceeds withdrawal are confirmed. A separate buyer in this new shop and C’s public-device action remain to be checked. This is not a mainnet launch or a completed audit.</p></div><div><span class="status beta">Mainnet pilot completed</span><h3>A small, real purchase cycle</h3><p>Original-token funding, a separate buyer’s purchase, pause, unsold-stock recovery and ETH collection were confirmed. The earlier pilot check ended paused and empty; the same V2 has since received production stock and opened. <a href="#funds">Check the receipts above ↗</a></p></div><div><span class="status live">Opened on Base</span><h3>First stock funded</h3><p>1,399,999 SOULI were deposited and the sale opened on October 4, 2026 at 05:29 UTC. With the prior one-token check, this fills the first 1.4M cumulative stock target. Check the purchase page for current stock and pause status. First stock may be replenished while selling, within the total cap. LP timing is not announced, and its beneficiary must be chosen before lock deployment. Completed V2 mobile purchase, pause, recovery and collection checks do not need to be repeated on the same unchanged release.</p></div></div><p>No independent audit report is published. Internal tests are useful evidence, not an audit or a guarantee against loss. No game release date, guaranteed liquidity, return or price appreciation is promised.</p><a class="button" href="/testnet/">Open the testnet playground ↗</a></section>

      <section id="sources"><p class="eyebrow">08 / ORIGINAL ROOTS. VISIBLE CHANGES.</p><h2>Read it. Check it.</h2><p>This game edition builds on the repository's original three-page technical note, <i>Souli: The ERC-20i Token With Native Inscriptions</i>, credited there to Todd Stool / ToddStool.eth. Its seed, dynamic/stable and layered-rendering ideas are retained; legacy naming, level counts and broad immutability language are not treated as proof of current deployed behavior.</p><ul class="source-list"><li><a href="https://github.com/ToddStool/fungi">FUNGI by Todd Stool · original art and contracts ↗</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/ToddStool/fungi-interface">Original FUNGI interface ↗</a></li><li><a href="/images/souli_whitepaper.pdf">Original technical PDF · historical reference ↗</a></li><li><a :href="'https://basescan.org/address/'+TOKEN">SOULI contract and transactions · Base ↗</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/yongchoi422/poopi_frontend">Original project repository ↗</a></li><li><a :href="'https://basescan.org/block/'+levels.block">Renderer level snapshot · October 1, 2026 ↗</a></li><li><a href="https://developers.uniswap.org/docs/protocols/v2/concepts/pools">Uniswap: pool ratios and LP ownership ↗</a></li></ul><p class="caption">The legacy docs.souli.net address currently leads to GitBook's management interface when checked. This page is the new public game guide; it does not alter the old GitBook account or its DNS.</p><div class="changelog"><b>v2.7 · October 4, 2026</b><p>Approved a 4.2M-token round with no calendar deadline and a 50% LP / 50% operations policy. Matching LP tokens are separate; full sellout needs 6.3M SOULI including LP stock. The first stock target is 1.4M with 700,000 separate LP tokens; the remaining 2.8M can be stocked progressively. The 50:50 policy continues throughout the round. V2 is deployed and source-matched on Sourcify; the fixed ETH price and completed mainnet cycle are now published. Both caps are 4.2M, including the one-token check. The one-year LP lock implementation passed internal local and Base-fork tests; public LP timing, beneficiary, deployment and funding remain pending. The new 3D game is labeled Cooking; original inscriptions remain available today. The completed small pilot receipts are retained. Production stock of 1,399,999 SOULI was deposited and the operator opened V2 on October 4, 2026 at 05:29 UTC. The separate approval, deposit and opening receipts are published. Current purchasing still requires available stock and an unpaused contract. See the purchase page for current status. No LP creation, funded lock or independent audit is claimed.</p></div><p class="last-line">GM, fren. Ask good questions. Check the receipts.</p></section>
